pert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Utah remains one of the most Republican states in presidential politics, and the 2028 race there is an open contest with no incumbent on either side. The state's partisan lean of roughly eleven points Republican, combined with double-digit Republican margins in recent presidential elections, forms the core of the projection. No public polls or expert ratings are yet available for the general election, so the forecast rests on fundamentals.\n\nHeadlines from Utah point to a Republican Party in transition but still dominant: potential successors to President Trump poll better in Utah than Trump does, and national outlets treat the state as a possible road map for the post-Trump GOP. Occasional commentary about Utah trending Democratic remains speculative. The Republican nominee starts as a clear favorite, with meaningful but not overwhelming uncertainty given the absence of polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1067, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1478, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1592, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1542, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1457, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.1497, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.1506, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.1453, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.1504, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.1517, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.1576, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.131, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.156, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.1532, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.1444, "m